From: Mathieu Laparie <mlaparie@disroot.org>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115-pro1x: Add NXP NFC controller

The Pro1X has an NXP NCI NFC controller on i2c1 at address 0x28.
Add a device tree node so the nxp-nci-i2c driver can probe it.

GPIO numbers from the stock vendor DTBO (Qualcomm bengal reference,
extracted from the dtbo_b partition):
  IRQ    = TLMM GPIO 70
  Enable = TLMM GPIO 69
  FW DL  = TLMM GPIO 31

The stock DTBO also defines a clock-request on GPIO 71, but that
conflicts with the touchscreen reset on the same pin in the mainline
DTS; NFC clock request is optional and omitted here.

Signed-off-by: Mathieu Laparie <mlaparie@disroot.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -133,6 +133,16 @@
 	status = "okay";

+	nfc@28 {
+		compatible = "nxp,nxp-nci-i2c";
+		reg = <0x28>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 70 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+
+		enable-gpios = <&tlmm 69 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		firmware-gpios = <&tlmm 31 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	};
+
 	pca9534: gpio@21 {
 		compatible = "nxp,pca9534";
 		reg = <0x21>;
